title: "Finite Contact Theory v0.7: The Taxonomy of Inevitability — A Program Map"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Douglas"
    given-names: "Seth"
    email: "apsiape@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4708-3252"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Apsiape/finite-contact-theory-public"
abstract: "A public release of Finite Contact Theory, a long-range finite reconstruction program, now spanning seven chapters on two axes. The quantum-facing axis grows the Bell/CHSH boundary, rational Born weights, a native carrier grammar, and an exact strict preparation gap from a finite one-use floor. The finite-epistemics axis publishes the identifiability and debt calculus (identification costs exactly ceil(log2 m) receipt bits and no symmetry-respecting rule can select), the inquiry calculus with its second law of asking (EC = H + KL + O), four theorems disassembling time (torsor origin-freedom, the helix covering, an arrow without thermodynamics, lawfulness without foundation), and a measured generative floor with an independent-implementation agreement. This v0.7 capstone chapter is the program map: three schema-level claim rows and a new live ceiling; ten dependency-free scripts verify the stack from a clean clone, and every unearned generalization is held open by name."
version: "0.7.0"
date-released: "2026-07-13"
